# Frontend environment (Vite). Copy to `.env.local` for development.
#
# You almost certainly do NOT need this file. Leaving VITE_API_BASE unset is
# the same as "same-origin", which is what both dev and production use:
#
#   - dev:        the Vite dev server proxies /api to http://127.0.0.1:8001
#                 (see vite.config.ts)
#   - production: Nginx proxies /api to uvicorn on the same origin
#                 (see ../nginx/balkan-fleet.conf.example)
#
# Same-origin means no CORS at all and a session cookie that just works.
#
# Set it only for a genuinely remote API on another origin:
#   VITE_API_BASE=https://api.example.com
# That is the one mode that falls back to an in-memory Bearer token, because a
# cross-site cookie cannot follow.
#
# If you point it at a loopback host instead of using the proxy, the host must
# MATCH your address bar — a page on localhost:3000 calling 127.0.0.1:8001 is
# cross-site for cookie purposes and SameSite=Strict drops the session silently.
